[CHOSEN, not recovered] vkd3d-shader 2.1 patch for the BF2 macOS port (LGPL-2.1+, as vkd3d).
vs_1_x relative addressing (c[a0.x + n]) has no separate address token; a0.x is
implied. vkd3d's own reader knows this (shader_sm1_read_param) but the writer always
emitted the token, which MojoShader and the D3D9 runtime read as a bogus instruction
("instruction token high bit must be zero"). BF2: skinning and indexed transforms.

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d-shader/d3dbc.c b/libs/vkd3d-shader/d3dbc.c
index 9ce1986..da8f161 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d-shader/d3dbc.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d-shader/d3dbc.c
@@ -2214,7 +2214,9 @@ static void d3dbc_write_instruction(struct d3dbc_compiler *compiler, const struc
 
         src = &ins->src[i];
         write_sm1_src_register(buffer, src);
-        if (src->reg.idx_count && src->reg.idx[0].rel_addr)
+        /* vs_1_x relative addressing has no address token: a0.x is implied
+         * (see shader_sm1_read_param()). */
+        if (src->reg.idx_count && src->reg.idx[0].rel_addr && version->major >= 2)
             write_sm1_src_register(buffer, src->reg.idx[0].rel_addr);
     }
 
